        "subject": "LU-20076 ptlrpc: retry soon when an OST refuses an MDT connect",
        "message": "LU-20076 ptlrpc: retry soon when an OST refuses an MDT connect\n\nAfter an OST restart, the MDT imports can reach it before it has\nfinished setting up and be refused with -EAGAIN. They then wait\nfor imperative recovery to report the OST back, about 2 seconds\nafter the mount on a test cluster, and the OST's recovery waits\nfor them.\n\nGive MDT to OST imports the quick retry that MDT to MDT imports\nhave. On a test cluster, OST0000 recovery after a remount took\n1.3 to 2.1 seconds without this and 1.1 to 1.2 seconds with it\nwhen the MDT connects were refused. Client imports are unchanged.\n\nSample ldiskfs DNE CI logs show 12 to 14 OST failovers in each\nrun of replay-ost-single, replay-single and recovery-small, and 5\nin replay-dual. At about 0.5 seconds each over the 25000 runs of\nthese suites in review testing in 30 days, this is an estimated\n40 suite-hours a month, an extrapolation, not a measured speedup.\n\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I2fe3f460844d68c0d013c90e2288c48b1e082faf\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
